<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34923" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">perflābĭlis</span></b> , e,
			adj.
		perflo. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Pass.</i>, <i>that can be blown
				through.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> Prop. (rare but class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">deos inducere perlucidos et perflabiles,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Div. 2, 17, 40</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sol. 27</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lacernae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 14, 6, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">locus,</span>”
				<i>exposed to the wind</i>, <i>airy</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 4, p. 150 <i>med.</i></span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Pall. 1, 36,
			3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			Fig., <i>susceptible</i> (postclass.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gentes perflabiles ad omnes dissensionum motus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 30, 7, 10</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>blowing through</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aër,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pall. 1, 6, 9</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">domus perflabili tinnitu fidium resultantes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 14, 6, 18</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
